1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,463
Take two numbers, four and nine.

2
00:00:02,463 --> 00:00:05,470
There are two different
ways to find a middle value.

3
00:00:05,870 --> 00:00:08,163
Aarav tried both in the study room.

4
00:00:08,163 --> 00:00:10,315
Add and halve: six and a half.

5
00:00:10,315 --> 00:00:13,082
Multiply, then take the square root: six.

6
00:00:13,532 --> 00:00:15,044
He tried more pairs.

7
00:00:15,044 --> 00:00:16,191
Two and eight.

8
00:00:16,191 --> 00:00:17,702
One and one hundred.

9
00:00:17,702 --> 00:00:20,208
The first way always won, or tied.

10
00:00:20,558 --> 00:00:23,197
Is that luck, or a rule that never breaks?

11
00:00:23,697 --> 00:00:24,927
It is a rule.

12
00:00:24,927 --> 00:00:29,433
Today we meet the geometric
mean, and the AMGM inequality.

13
00:00:30,083 --> 00:00:32,314
First, what is a geometric mean?

14
00:00:32,314 --> 00:00:35,393
Think of a rectangle,
four wide and nine tall.

15
00:00:35,393 --> 00:00:37,034
Its area is thirty six.

16
00:00:37,434 --> 00:00:39,919
Now find a square with the same area.

17
00:00:39,919 --> 00:00:43,444
Its side is six, because
six times six is thirty six.

18
00:00:43,844 --> 00:00:46,117
That side is the geometric mean.

19
00:00:46,117 --> 00:00:50,590
For two positive numbers a and
b, G is the square root of a b.

20
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:53,111
And a, G, b make a GP.

21
00:00:53,111 --> 00:00:54,432
Four, six, nine.

22
00:00:54,432 --> 00:00:57,970
Six over four and nine over
six are both one and a half.

23
00:00:58,570 --> 00:01:00,735
We can fit in more than one.

24
00:01:00,735 --> 00:01:05,661
To put n geometric means between a
and b, we need n plus one equal jumps

25
00:01:05,661 --> 00:01:06,561
of r.

26
00:01:06,709 --> 00:01:10,991
NCERT's example: three means between
one and two hundred and fifty six.

27
00:01:10,991 --> 00:01:15,405
That is four jumps, so r to the four
is two hundred and fifty six, and

28
00:01:15,405 --> 00:01:16,305
r is four.

29
00:01:16,876 --> 00:01:19,790
The means are four,
sixteen and sixty four.

30
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:21,340
Quick one.

31
00:01:21,205 --> 00:01:23,967
What is the geometric
mean of two and eighteen?

32
00:01:23,967 --> 00:01:25,049
Pause and think.

33
00:01:28,249 --> 00:01:29,149
Six.

34
00:01:28,704 --> 00:01:32,713
Two times eighteen is thirty six,
and the square root of thirty six is

35
00:01:32,713 --> 00:01:33,613
six.

36
00:01:33,819 --> 00:01:35,162
Now the big race.

37
00:01:35,162 --> 00:01:39,003
Keep the total fixed at ten,
so the AM stays at five.

38
00:01:39,003 --> 00:01:40,757
Change a, and watch G.

39
00:01:41,157 --> 00:01:44,032
When a is one and b is nine, G is three.

40
00:01:44,032 --> 00:01:46,907
When a is two and b is eight, G is four.

41
00:01:47,307 --> 00:01:50,880
As the two numbers come
closer, G climbs towards A.

42
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,993
At five and five, they meet.

43
00:01:52,993 --> 00:01:53,893
G equals A.

44
00:01:53,789 --> 00:01:55,258
But G never gets past A.

45
00:01:55,908 --> 00:01:57,442
Why can G never win?

46
00:01:57,442 --> 00:02:00,191
Here is the proof, in four small steps.

47
00:02:00,591 --> 00:02:01,491
Step one.

48
00:02:01,372 --> 00:02:05,519
A minus G is a plus b over two,
minus the square root of a b.

49
00:02:06,269 --> 00:02:07,169
Step two.

50
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:08,611
Put it all over two.

51
00:02:08,611 --> 00:02:11,585
The top is a plus b, minus two root a b.

52
00:02:12,335 --> 00:02:13,235
Step three.

53
00:02:13,218 --> 00:02:15,195
That top is a perfect square.

54
00:02:15,195 --> 00:02:18,265
It is root a minus root
b, the whole squared.

55
00:02:19,015 --> 00:02:19,915
Step four.

56
00:02:19,872 --> 00:02:21,744
A square is never negative.

57
00:02:21,744 --> 00:02:23,891
So A minus G is zero or more.

58
00:02:23,891 --> 00:02:25,221
A is at least G.

59
00:02:25,971 --> 00:02:29,189
And A equals G only when
root a equals root b.

60
00:02:29,189 --> 00:02:30,843
That means a equals b.

61
00:02:31,493 --> 00:02:32,544
Side by side.

62
00:02:32,544 --> 00:02:35,084
The arithmetic mean adds, then halves.

63
00:02:35,084 --> 00:02:37,546
For four and nine, six and a half.

64
00:02:37,946 --> 00:02:41,240
The geometric mean multiplies,
then takes the square root.

65
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:42,804
For four and nine, six.

66
00:02:42,804 --> 00:02:45,489
Numbers far apart make
a big gap between them.

67
00:02:46,089 --> 00:02:46,989
Your turn.

68
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:49,544
Two positive numbers have an AM of ten.

69
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:51,253
Can their GM be twelve?

70
00:02:51,253 --> 00:02:52,414
Pause and think.

71
00:02:55,614 --> 00:02:56,514
No.

72
00:02:56,034 --> 00:02:57,966
G can never be bigger than A.

73
00:02:57,966 --> 00:02:59,998
Their GM must be ten or less.

74
00:03:00,648 --> 00:03:01,708
Remember this.

75
00:03:01,708 --> 00:03:05,800
For positive numbers, the AM
is never smaller than the GM.

76
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:08,190
Now, one worked example.

77
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:12,864
The AM of two positive numbers
is ten, and their GM is eight.

78
00:03:12,864 --> 00:03:14,122
Find the numbers.

79
00:03:14,622 --> 00:03:15,522
Step one.

80
00:03:15,465 --> 00:03:18,459
The AM is ten, so a plus b is twenty.

81
00:03:19,209 --> 00:03:20,109
Step two.

82
00:03:20,036 --> 00:03:23,021
The GM is eight, so a b is sixty four.

83
00:03:23,771 --> 00:03:24,728
Step three.

84
00:03:24,728 --> 00:03:29,714
They are the roots of x squared, minus
twenty x, plus sixty four, equals

85
00:03:29,714 --> 00:03:30,614
zero.

86
00:03:31,047 --> 00:03:31,989
Step four.

87
00:03:31,989 --> 00:03:35,831
This factors as x minus
four, times x minus sixteen.

88
00:03:36,581 --> 00:03:38,733
So the numbers are four and sixteen.

89
00:03:38,733 --> 00:03:42,994
Check: their average is ten, and the
square root of sixty four is eight.

90
00:03:43,644 --> 00:03:45,106
Now, the exam trap.

91
00:03:45,456 --> 00:03:48,086
Students use AMGM on any numbers.

92
00:03:48,086 --> 00:03:50,228
Try minus two and minus eight.

93
00:03:50,628 --> 00:03:55,093
Their AM is minus five, but the
square root of their product is four.

94
00:03:55,093 --> 00:03:56,202
Four is bigger!

95
00:03:56,202 --> 00:03:58,758
The rule only works for positive numbers.

96
00:03:59,408 --> 00:04:00,901
Where is this asked?

97
00:04:00,901 --> 00:04:01,934
In JEE Main.

98
00:04:01,934 --> 00:04:06,304
In April twenty twenty three, a paper
inserted arithmetic and geometric

99
00:04:06,304 --> 00:04:09,080
means between two numbers and linked them.

100
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:10,935
Exam level now.

101
00:04:10,935 --> 00:04:15,987
For x greater than zero, what is the
smallest value of x plus sixteen over

102
00:04:15,987 --> 00:04:16,887
x?

103
00:04:16,423 --> 00:04:17,732
Pause and solve.

104
00:04:23,132 --> 00:04:24,589
The answer is B.

105
00:04:24,589 --> 00:04:25,489
Eight.

106
00:04:25,777 --> 00:04:30,661
x and sixteen over x are both
positive, so AM is at least GM.

107
00:04:31,161 --> 00:04:35,021
Their GM is the square root
of x times sixteen over x.

108
00:04:35,021 --> 00:04:37,645
That is root sixteen, which is four.

109
00:04:38,145 --> 00:04:41,505
So their sum is at least
two times four, eight.

110
00:04:41,505 --> 00:04:46,127
It is exactly eight when x equals
sixteen over x, at x equals four.

111
00:04:46,727 --> 00:04:48,267
Here is your recap.

112
00:04:48,267 --> 00:04:49,850
Screenshot this card.

113
00:04:53,050 --> 00:04:55,236
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

114
00:04:55,636 --> 00:04:56,536
One.

115
00:04:56,108 --> 00:04:59,157
Find the geometric mean
of three and twenty seven.

116
00:05:00,057 --> 00:05:00,957
Two.

117
00:05:00,493 --> 00:05:02,466
Why must both numbers be positive?

118
00:05:03,366 --> 00:05:04,266
Three.

119
00:05:03,899 --> 00:05:06,083
When is the AM equal to the GM?

120
00:05:07,183 --> 00:05:10,559
Next time: one, plus
four, plus nine, and on.

121
00:05:10,559 --> 00:05:12,983
Can one formula add all the squares?

122
00:05:12,983 --> 00:05:14,798
The sum of special series.
